    Bug 1693772 - Attempt to fix timeout of browser_formPickers.js. r=aleca


    I have been analyzing the timeout and see it happen mainly when the
    datetime picker should show up. The click seems to be ignored. One
    option would be to re-trigger the click in these cases, but that did not
    work reliably and was causing other issues. Adding a small delay before
    issuing the click worked better.

    A different timeout was observed when running the test with --verify,
    which sometimes even leads to a crash/hang: In the mailbox case, calling
    `input.showPicker()`, the picker opened as a blank square and
    `BrowserTestUtils.waitForDateTimePickerPanelShown()` either fulfills
    very (very!) late, or crashes. This is not fixed by this patch, but was
    also not observed on CI.

    Adding some log messages to see the location of the timeout, in case the
    intermittent is not fully fixed.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D227711

diff --git a/mail/base/test/widgets/browser_formPickers.js b/mail/base/test/widgets/browser_formPickers.js
index 678ac609980..e225c7ce2c5 100644
--- a/mail/base/test/widgets/browser_formPickers.js
+++ b/mail/base/test/widgets/browser_formPickers.js
@@ -33,10 +33,15 @@ async function checkABrowser(browser) {

   // Date picker

-  // Open the popup.
+  // Open the popup. Sometimes the click to open the date picker is ignored and
+  // the test runs into a timeout. Adding a small delay here helps to prevent that.
+  // eslint-disable-next-line mozilla/no-arbitrary-setTimeout
+  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 250));
+  info("Preparing to open the date picker.");
   const pickerPromise = BrowserTestUtils.waitForDateTimePickerPanelShown(
     win.top
   );
+
   await SpecialPowers.spawn(browser, [], function () {
     const input = content.document.querySelector(`input[type="date"]`);
     if (content.location.protocol == "mailbox:") {
@@ -52,6 +57,7 @@ async function checkABrowser(browser) {
     }
   });
   const picker = await pickerPromise;
+  Assert.ok(!!picker, "Date picker was successfully opened");

   // Click in the middle of the picker. This should always land on a date and
   // close the picker.
